  "finding": [
    "LibreDWG observes the same two layout bodies and block associations in originals and same-writer resaves; the original root lacks ACAD_LAYOUT, while each resave links its existing two-member dictionary.",
    "The supplied ODA DXFs for the originals use newly created layout handles, whereas the resaved-input outputs retain selected layout handles and all four retain selected BLOCK_RECORD handles. Physical DXF backlinks and loaded reciprocal links agree with zero ezdxf audit errors or repairs.",
    "The source model LAYOUT has a null last-active viewport, but each supplied DXF has a non-null model viewport. ODA output therefore cannot be used as evidence that the entire source layout graph was preserved without transformation.",
    "The audit rejects a changed DWG hash and a physically modified DXF BLOCK_RECORD backlink, preserves a preexisting result, and succeeds on corrected retry."
  ],
